type: software
title: "Rational Fibonacci–Catalan polynomials: positivity, a Coxeter classification and q-Fibonomial unimodality up to width seven"
abstract: "Unrefereed research candidate. For every pair (m,n), the reduced denominator of the rational q-Fibonacci–Catalan function C_{m,n} is exactly [F_gcd(m,n)]_q and the reduced numerator is the Hilbert series of an Artinian weighted complete intersection, so C_{m,n} has nonnegative coefficients whenever gcd(m,n) <= 2. The same holds for Lucas sequences with coprime positive parameters. For the Fibonacci quotient of every irreducible finite reflection group the polynomial shifts are classified and all are positive. The q-Fibonomial coefficients are unimodal whenever the smaller index is at most seven, on a set of density about 0.408, and for each fixed width once the larger index is large."
